    "Dry Bulk Freight": "Capesize: The Capesize C5TC average closed the week at USD 35,457/day. Trip from Continent to F.East is down by 1.6k/day at USD 71,722/day, Transatlantic R/V is lower by 0.3k/day at USD 44,566/day, and Bolivar to Rotterdam is higher by 0.3k/day at USD 49,894/day, while Transpacific R/ V is increased by 1.7k/day at USD 35,918/day. Trip from Tubarao to Rotterdam is increased by 0.6k/ day at USD 28,509/day, China-Brazil R/V is lower by 0.9k/day at USD 37,208/day, and & trip from Saldanha Bay to Qinqdao is increased by 0.6k/day at USD 28,509/day.\n\nKamsarmax/Panamax: The Kamsarmax P5TC Timecharter average started the week at USD 18,213/day closing with an increase at USD 18,780/day. Trip from Skaw-Gib to F.East is im- proved by 1.4k/day at USD 30,840/day, Pacific R/ Vis up by 0.6k/day at USD 15,168/day, while Transatlantic R/V is increased by 1.1k/day at USD 21,205/day, and Singapore R/V via Atlantic is de- creased by 0.4k/day at USD 18,052/day.\n\nUltramax/Supramax: The Ultramax S11TC average closed the week about USD 1.1k/day lower than its opening at USD 20,336/day. The Supramax S10TC average closed the week about 1.1k/day lower than its opening at USD 18,302/day. The Baltic Supramax Asia S3TC average closed the week about 1.3k/day lower than previous week at USD 17,754/day. N.China one Australian or Pacific R/V is declined by 1.7k/day at USD 16,950/day, USG to Skaw Passero is softer by 2.1k/day at USD 27,311/day. S.China trip via Indonesia to EC India is down by 1.3k/day at USD 21,486/day, trip from S.China via Indonesia to S.China pays USD 15,063/day, while Med/B.Sea to China/S.Korea is reduced by 0.4k/day at USD 26,265/day.\n\nHandysize: The Handysize HS7TC average closed the week reduced by 0.3k/day at USD 15,969/day. Skaw-Passero trip to Boston-Galveston pays 0.1k/ day less at USD 11,221/day, Brazil to Cont. pays 0.8k/day less at USD 20,911/day, S.E. Asia trip to Spore/Japan 0.1k/day is softer at USD 17,238/day, China/S.Korea/Japan round trip is reduced at USD 17,156/day, and trip from U.S. Gulf to Cont. is re- duced by 1.4k/day at USD 18,254/day, while N.China-S.Korea-Japan trip to S.E.Asia is reduced by 0.1k/day at USD 17,169/day.",
    "Tanker Freight": "VLCC: average T/CE ended the week up by 30k/ day at USD 223,340/day. Middle East Gulf to China trip is up by 47.4k/day at USD 428,151/day. West Africa to China trip is up by 19.5k/day at USD 116,661/day and US Gulf to China trip is up by 23.2k/day at USD 125,209/day.\n\nSuezmax: average T/CE closed the week firmer by 55.3k/day at USD 209,325/day. West Africa to Continent trip is down by 6.7k/day at USD 98,065/ day, Black Sea to Mediterranean is up by 117.2k/ day at USD 320,585/day, and Middle East Gulf to Med trip is improved by 1.7k/day at USD 318,930/ day, while trip from Guyana to ARA is reduced by 7.1k/day at USD 99,757/day.\n\nAframax: average T/CE closed the week lower by 21.8k/day at USD 88,634/day. North Sea to Conti- nent trip is down by 22.9k/day at USD 106,771/ day, Kuwait to Singapore is up by 2k/day at USD 75,505/day, while route from Caribbean to US Gulf trip is down by 28.5k/day at USD 112,909/ day. Trip from South East Asia to East Coast Aus- tralia is down by 1k/day at USD 23,414/day & Cross Mediterranean trip is down by 55.8k/day at USD 102,993/day. US Gulf to UK-Continent is re- duced by 21.2k/day at USD 102,727/day and the East Coast Mexico to US Gulf trip is down by USD 30.2k/day at USD 122,459/day.\n\nProducts: The LR2 route (TC1) Middle East to Ja- pan is this week higher by 3k/day at USD 135,472/ day. Trip from (TC15) Med to Far East has in- creased by 7.5k/day at USD 36,203/day and (TC20) AG to UK Continent is down by 7.5k/day at USD 113,466/day. The LR1 route (TC5) from Middle East Gulf to Japan is up by 1.6k/day at USD 99,474/day, while the (TC8) Middle East Gulf to UK -Continent is down by 7.5k/day at USD 113,466/ day and the (TC16) Amsterdam to Lome trip is im- proved at USD /day. The MR Atlantic Basket is in- creased by 7k/day at USD 46,472/day & the MR Pacific Basket earnings are lower by at USD 23,744/day. The MR route from Rotterdam to New York (TC2) is firmer by 3k/day at USD 135,472/day, (TC6) Intermed (Alger